{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1726","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1726","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1726\",\"parent_revision\":\"3066a60d57bf8b17a48085d7a70ac87c5b412e8ea2f981d9d5e2d3ed0da57933\",\"root_revision\":\"3066a60d57bf8b17a48085d7a70ac87c5b412e8ea2f981d9d5e2d3ed0da57933\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\nAll conditions AVAILABLE:\\n- Functional intent: determine GitHub Gist PATCH behavior when filename key is new (not matching any existing file)\\n- Scope: live API probe + record findings + update #1724\\n- External interface: `PATCH /gists/{gist_id}` via `gh api` and PyGithub `Gist.edit()`\\n- Constraints: requires `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `gist` OAuth scope\\n- Existing system context: `artifact_provider.py:529` \u2014 `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` is the exact call path in question\\n- Verification: item already specifies the exact `gh api` command to run and expected evidence\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-13)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 This question has two active implications:\\n1. Blocking #1724 (chunked-append design): the architecture depends on whether PATCH creates new files.\\n2. Active production risk in `store_artifact_content` today: `artifact_provider.py:529` calls `gist.edit()` with sanitized paths that do not match existing gist files on first write. If option 2 (silent ignore) is the server behavior, every artifact write silently discards content \u2014 a current production defect, not a hypothetical.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Chunked-append design in #1724 \u2014 the write path architecture depends entirely on PATCH behavior for new filename keys\\n- Active production risk: `store_artifact_content` (`artifact_provider.py:529`) already calls `gist.edit()` with filename keys that likely do not exist in the gist yet\\n- Bottleneck: Artifact storage reliability cannot be verified until the API behavior is known\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Option 3 (silent create): `store_artifact_content` already works; #1724 can proceed with per-chunk-file layout\\n- Option 1 (422 error): Production bug confirmed and scoped \u2014 pre-create step required before `gist.edit()`\\n- Option 2 (silent ignore): Production bug confirmed \u2014 silent data loss on every first artifact write; fix must be filed immediately\\n- All outcomes: Ambiguity resolved; #1724 can be planned; artifact storage reliability known\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nPer GitHub REST API docs, each key in the PATCH `files` dict must match the current filename of an existing file. The documented use cases are: update (same key, new `content`), rename (same key, new `content` + `filename`), delete (same key, `null`). New-file creation via PATCH is not documented. Actual server behavior is one of:\\n1. Returns 422 Unprocessable Entity \u2014 whole PATCH fails\\n2. Silently ignores the unknown key, updating only matching keys\\n3. Silently creates the new file (undocumented)\\n\\nPyGithub `Gist.edit()` passes the dict verbatim through `InputFileContent._identity` \u2014 whatever the server does is exactly what `store_artifact_content` at `artifact_provider.py:529` experiences today.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- Research note at `.tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-gist-patch-new-filename.md`: exact commands run, full response JSON, date, one-sentence conclusion\\n- Issue #1724 updated with verified behavior in its Evidence section\\n- If option 2 (silent ignore): bug backlog item filed for `store_artifact_content` silently discarding first-write artifact content\\n- If option 1 (422 error): bug backlog item filed for `store_artifact_content` raising unhandled `GithubException` on every first write to a new artifact path\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. A live `gh api -X PATCH /gists/{gist_id}` call is run against a throwaway gist with a filename key that does not exist in the gist.\\n2. HTTP status code and response body are recorded verbatim in `.tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-gist-patch-new-filename.md`.\\n3. A subsequent `GET /gists/{gist_id}` confirms whether the new file was created, ignored, or an error occurred.\\n4. Issue #1724 is updated with a one-sentence summary of the verified behavior.\\n5. If option 2 (silent ignore): a bug backlog item is filed for `store_artifact_content` silently discarding new artifact file writes.\\n6. If option 1 (422 error): a bug backlog item is filed for `store_artifact_content` raising an unhandled `GithubException` on every first write to a new artifact path.\\n7. If option 3 (silent create): a note confirms `store_artifact_content` works correctly for first writes and #1724 can proceed with per-chunk-file layout.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Code | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` line 529 \u2014 `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` |\\n| Code | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` lines 195-209 \u2014 `_sanitize_gist_filename` |\\n| Code | `.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/github/Gist.py` lines 246-263 \u2014 `Gist.edit()` passes `_identity` dict verbatim to PATCH |\\n| Code | `.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/github/InputFileContent.py` lines 44-62 \u2014 `InputFileContent._identity` contains only `content` (and optionally `filename`) |\\n| API docs | https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists?apiVersion=2022-11-28 \u2014 \\\"Update a gist\\\" endpoint |\\n| Related item | #1724 \u2014 No way to append to artifacts in small chunks |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `gist` OAuth scope in the environment where the probe is run\\n- Blocks: #1724 (chunked-append design \u2014 write path architecture depends on PATCH behavior for new filename keys)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 a single shell session (~10 minutes). Exact commands specified in Reproducibility section. Only prerequisite is `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `gist` scope.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- `GITHUB_TOKEN` must have `gist` scope \u2014 standard PATs and GITHUB_ACTIONS tokens may lack this scope\\n- Live API call required \u2014 cannot be answered from static analysis of the codebase or API docs alone\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- The exact `gh api` commands run, with full response JSON recorded verbatim\\n- HTTP status code from the PATCH call\\n- File list from the subsequent GET \u2014 whether `new-file.md` appears, is absent, or an error occurred\\n- Date and `GITHUB_TOKEN` scope used\\n- Saved to `.tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-gist-patch-new-filename.md`\\n- One-sentence conclusion: which of the three behaviors (422 error / silent ignore / silent create) was observed\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Source |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Determine which of three server behaviors occurs when PATCH /gists/{id} receives a filename key not present in the gist |\\n| Scope | AVAILABLE | Live API probe + record findings + update #1724 |\\n| External interface | AVAILABLE | `PATCH /gists/{gist_id}` via `gh api` and PyGithub `Gist.edit()` |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Requires `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `gist` OAuth scope |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `artifact_provider.py:529` \u2014 `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` is the exact call path |\\n| Verification | AVAILABLE | Exact `gh api` commands specified; expected evidence defined |\\n\\nAll conditions AVAILABLE. No MISSING or BLOCKED conditions.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Verify `GITHUB_TOKEN` has `gist` OAuth scope (Settings > Developer settings > Personal access tokens > `gist` checkbox).\\n2. Create a throwaway gist with one file:\\n   ```bash\\n   GIST_ID=$(gh api /gists -X POST -f 'description=test-gist-patch-behavior' -f 'public=false' -F 'files[existing-file.md][content]=hello' --jq '.id')\\n   echo \\\"Gist ID: $GIST_ID\\\"\\n   ```\\n3. PATCH with a key that does NOT match the existing filename:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID -X PATCH -F 'files[new-file.md][content]=world'\\n   ```\\n4. Read back the gist to observe its file list:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID --jq '.files | keys'\\n   ```\\n5. Record HTTP status code, response body, and final file list verbatim.\\n6. If `new-file.md` was created, confirm multi-file creation in a single request:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID -X PATCH -F 'files[another-new-file.md][content]=test'\\n   ```\\n7. Delete the throwaway gist:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID -X DELETE\\n   ```\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPer GitHub REST API docs, each key in the PATCH `files` dict must match the current filename of an existing file. The documented use cases are: update (same key, new `content`), rename (same key, new `content` + `filename`), delete (same key, `null`). New-file creation via PATCH is not documented. Actual server behavior is one of:\\n1. Returns 422 Unprocessable Entity \u2014 whole PATCH fails\\n2. Silently ignores the unknown key, updating only matching keys\\n3. Silently creates the new file (undocumented)\\n\\nPyGithub `Gist.edit()` passes the dict verbatim through `InputFileContent._identity` \u2014 whatever the server does is exactly what `store_artifact_content` at `artifact_provider.py:529` experiences today.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Web research 2026-04-12 \u2014 pygithub-gist-research.md (Q1c)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **unknown: does gist patch create a new file when the filename key does not exist?** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Blocks: Chunked-append design in #1724 \u2014 the write path architecture depends entirely on PATCH behavior for new filename keys\\n- Active production risk: `store_artifact_content` (`artifact_provider.py:529`) already calls `gist.edit()` with filename keys that likely do not exist in the gist yet\\n- Bottleneck: Artifact storage reliability cannot be verified until the API behavior is known\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Structure\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Research note at `.tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-gist-patch-new-filename.md`: exact commands run, full response JSON, date, one-sentence conclusion\\n- Issue #1724 updated with verified behavior in its Evidence section\\n- If option 2 (silent ignore): bug backlog item filed for `store_artifact_content` silently discarding first-write artifact content\\n- If option 1 (422 error): bug backlog item filed for `store_artifact_content` raising unhandled `GithubException` on every first write to a new artifact path\\n</div>\\n\\n## Rt-Ica Assessment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Source |\\n|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Determine which of three server behaviors occurs when PATCH /gists/{id} receives a filename key not present in the gist |\\n| Scope | AVAILABLE | Live API probe + record findings + update #1724 |\\n| External interface | AVAILABLE | `PATCH /gists/{gist_id}` via `gh api` and PyGithub `Gist.edit()` |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Requires `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `gist` OAuth scope |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | `artifact_provider.py:529` \u2014 `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` is the exact call path |\\n| Verification | AVAILABLE | 