s two active implications:\\n1. Blocking #1724 (chunked-append design): the architecture depends on whether PATCH creates new files.\\n2. Active production risk in `store_artifact_content` today: `artifact_provider.py:529` calls `gist.edit()` with sanitized paths that do not match existing gist files on first write. If option 2 (silent ignore) is the server behavior, every artifact write silently discards content \u2014 a current production defect, not a hypothetical.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Blockers\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `GITHUB_TOKEN` must have `gist` scope \u2014 standard PATs and GITHUB_ACTIONS tokens may lack this scope\\n- Live API call required \u2014 cannot be answered from static analysis of the codebase or API docs alone\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/pygithub-gist-research.md` \u00a7Q1c (BLOCKED in web research)\\n- https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists?apiVersion=2022-11-28\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Verify `GITHUB_TOKEN` has `gist` OAuth scope (Settings > Developer settings > Personal access tokens > `gist` checkbox).\\n2. Create a throwaway gist with one file:\\n   ```bash\\n   GIST_ID=$(gh api /gists -X POST -f 'description=test-gist-patch-behavior' -f 'public=false' -F 'files[existing-file.md][content]=hello' --jq '.id')\\n   echo \\\"Gist ID: $GIST_ID\\\"\\n   ```\\n3. PATCH with a key that does NOT match the existing filename:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID -X PATCH -F 'files[new-file.md][content]=world'\\n   ```\\n4. Read back the gist to observe its file list:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID --jq '.files | keys'\\n   ```\\n5. Record HTTP status code, response body, and final file list verbatim.\\n6. If `new-file.md` was created, confirm multi-file creation in a single request:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID -X PATCH -F 'files[another-new-file.md][content]=test'\\n   ```\\n7. Delete the throwaway gist:\\n   ```bash\\n   gh api /gists/$GIST_ID -X DELETE\\n   ```\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why This Blocks Other Work\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe chunked-append design (issue for \\\"No way to append to artifacts in small chunks\\\") depends on this answer. If PATCH creates files, a per-chunk-file layout (`plan/architect-foo.part-001.md`, `...part-002.md`, ...) is trivial \u2014 the producer just PATCHes a new key per chunk. If PATCH does not create files, every first chunk for a new artifact needs a separate create-gist or create-file path, and the chunk-append semantics change.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: `GITHUB_TOKEN` with `gist` OAuth scope in the environment where the probe is run\\n- Blocks: #1724 (chunked-append design \u2014 write path architecture depends on PATCH behavior for new filename keys)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Option 3 (silent create): `store_artifact_content` already works; #1724 can proceed with per-chunk-file layout\\n- Option 1 (422 error): Production bug confirmed and scoped \u2014 pre-create step required before `gist.edit()`\\n- Option 2 (silent ignore): Production bug confirmed \u2014 silent data loss on every first artifact write; fix must be filed immediately\\n- All outcomes: Ambiguity resolved; #1724 can be planned; artifact storage reliability known\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-05-08T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Code | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` line 529 \u2014 `gist.edit(files={filename: InputFileContent(content)})` |\\n| Code | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` lines 195-209 \u2014 `_sanitize_gist_filename` |\\n| Code | `.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/github/Gist.py` lines 246-263 \u2014 `Gist.edit()` passes `_identity` dict verbatim to PATCH |\\n| Code | `.venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/github/InputFileContent.py` lines 44-62 \u2014 `InputFileContent._identity` contains only `content` (and optionally `filename`) |\\n| API docs | https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists?apiVersion=2022-11-28 \u2014 \\\"Update a gist\\\" endpoint |\\n| Related item | #1724 \u2014 No way to append to artifacts in small chunks |\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe GitHub REST API documentation for \\\"Update a gist\\\" states: *\\\"The gist files to be updated, renamed, or deleted. Each key must match the current filename (including extension) of the targeted gist file.\\\"* (https://docs.github.com/en/rest/gists/gists \u2014 accessed 2026-04-12)\\n\\nThe docs do not state what happens when a caller violates this rule by passing a key that does not match any existing file. Three behaviors are plausible:\\n\\n1. The server returns a 422 error and the whole PATCH fails.\\n2. The server silently ignores the unknown key and updates only the matching ones.\\n3. The server silently creates the new file (undocumented but functionally useful).\\n\\nPyGithub passes the dict through verbatim (`Gist.py` \u2192 `InputFileContent._identity` \u2192 PATCH body), so its behavior is whatever the server does.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a279b480fd40d86891be49010ef78f4c627c33abfbe340786ff2c68ada60bd00\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS-PmA\"}"}